---
source: crates/odx-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: cmd.render_long_help().to_string()
---
Compare what two environments run, addon by addon

Usage: odx env diff [OPTIONS] <A> <B>

Arguments:
  <A>
          First environment, or a branch of one

  <B>
          Second environment, or a branch of one

Options:
  -C, --project-dir <DIR>
          Run as if started in DIR

      --remote <NAME>
          The remote whose branches are compared (local branches when it has none)
          
          [default: origin]

  -c, --config <FILE>
          The pyproject.toml or repos.yaml to use

      --vendored <A> <B>
          Compare two vendor manifests (`.odx/vendor.lock`) of the environments instead

      --installed <A> <B>
          Compare the wheels installed in two virtual environments (or site-packages) instead

  -j, --jobs <N>
          Override the number of parallel jobs

      --offline
          Serve forge and index data from the cache only. Only network calls are skipped: local work (git, pre-commit, odoo-lint) takes as long as before

      --fresh
          Ignore cached data; refresh everything before answering

      --no-refresh
          Use cached data even when stale. Like --offline, this saves network time only

      --refresh-index
          Rebuild the addon index for the series involved

      --json
          Machine-readable output on stdout

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase log verbosity (repeatable)

  -q, --quiet
          Errors only

  -h, --help
          Print help

  -V, --version
          Print version
